key|name|url|evidence
pearling|Abu Dhabi Culture — Pearl diving|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/pearl-diving|Main season Ghous Al Kabir June to September; nukhadh manages boat and profits; sardal fleet captain; seib handles diver ropes; tabbabs assist; ridha serve; naham sings; deyeen oyster bag; zubail weight rope; yada ascent rope; fattam nose clip.
divingtools|Abu Dhabi Culture — Diving equipment|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/diving-equipment-in-the-past|Maflaqa curved oyster knife; khabt leather finger protection; balad stone or lead descent weight; shamshool diving clothing; taqiya protection from jellyfish locally doll.
maritime|Abu Dhabi Culture — Maritime life|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/maritime-life|Boum merchant vessel; saffar vessel for long trading voyages; qatta vessel for short trips; jalibut bakara sanbock pearling/passengers; hoori fishing; cotton seals plank gaps; palm-fibre rope; lime called noora.
burqa|Abu Dhabi Culture — Burqa|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/burqa|Traditional fabric face mask; associated with married women; quraizah burqa artisans; lining al sheel imported India; red lining highest quality; seif wood bridge over nose; shubuq tie; gold circles and stars bridal decorations.
karrey|Abu Dhabi Culture — Karrey|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/karrey|Karrey leases camels and carries luggage lekshar for summer mukaid movement from hot to cooler areas; women arranged travel while men departed for diving; Al Ain and Liwa oasis destinations.
tannaf|Abu Dhabi Culture — Tannaf|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/tannaf|Tannaf leads camel caravans using safe route knowledge; also hired camel herder.
saqa|Abu Dhabi Culture — Saqa|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/the-saqa|Animal-hide milk-churning bag; mouth waja; tripod tarjabah also shayb; hides salted then tanned; churning separates butter.
taresh|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Taresh|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/al-taresh|Messenger delivers oral/written messages; khareetah protective bag; honesty and eloquence valued.
baydar|Abu Dhabi Culture — Baydar|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/baydar|Agricultural worker tending another owner's palms; paid money or share of crop; landowner called hanjari.
fishing|Abu Dhabi Culture — Fishing equipment|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/fishing-equipment|Leekh gill net; sharkh coastal low tide set rising tide traps fish; saleya single-person round cast net weighted with lead; gargoor hemispherical wire trap; hadaq hook and line; yall fine net sardines and anchovies; saragh shore rope; kufa weight sanjal.
kami|Abu Dhabi Culture — Kami|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/kami|Traditional dairy curd eaten with dates and ghee; drying preserves surplus without refrigeration; dried yaqt derivative.
shilla|Abu Dhabi Culture — Shilla|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/shilla|Sung Nabati poetry accompanied by rebabah; descriptive praise and wisdom themes; one or two performers.
jafeer|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Jafeer|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/al-jafeer|Palm basket two handles; coastal fish/desert dates; base badwah; sewn spirally; taller than arm called mizmah.
raha|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Raha|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/al-raha|Two round stone grain mill; upper rotates; hadi handle; qutb axis; thifal woven cloth receives flour; lahwa grain portion; tarsha heavy mill worked by two women.
saj|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Saj|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/al-saj|Circular iron or aluminium bread griddle; also toubi; raqaq bread cooked on it.
bisht|Abu Dhabi Culture — Bisht|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/bisht|Men's ceremonial outer cloak; wool texture summer light/winter heavy; desert blanket; Najafi Najaf Iraq; Hasawi Al Ahsa; Doranki two-coloured; Nizwani Nizwa; darbawiya hand tailoring with zari.
khabees|Abu Dhabi Culture — Khabees|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/khabees|Toasted flour dessert sweetened with sugar or honey; ghee cardamom saffron rose water; flour toasted before liquid.
rigag|Abu Dhabi Culture — Rigag|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/rigag|Wafer-thin bread cooked hot pan; flour water salt no yeast; mhyawa fish paste topping; used in stews in Ramadan.
smith|Abu Dhabi Culture — Blacksmithing|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/blacksmithing|Tannour furnace; menfakh sheepskin and wood bellows; anvil shaping iron; melqat hot metal tongs; bawera anchor; maker stamps identify work; water hardens metal.
utensils|Abu Dhabi Culture — Cooking utensils|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/cooking-utensils|Tabi frying pan; malas stirring ladle; mashkhala strainer also musfat; gafsha large serving spoon also khashoga; mihmas iron coffee-roasting stirrer; RAK clay kilns.
sandalwood|Abu Dhabi Culture — Sandalwood|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/sandalwood|Aromatic wood from eastern India; used in incense; bidaa hair perfume contains sandalwood wars and rose extract. Medical claims excluded.
isqa|Abu Dhabi Culture — Palm isqa|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/uses-of-palm-isqa|Date stalk after fruit removal; tarqiana makes clapping sound; nashaba bow from curved stalk; shamarikh tied as broom.
pottery|Abu Dhabi Culture — Pottery|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/pottery|Clay vessels; hib cools water; kharas stores dates or dried fish; evidence from third millennium BCE.
harees|Abu Dhabi Culture — Harees|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/harees|Wheat soaked overnight then cooked with meat; medrab or mesdam wooden beating tool; ghee added; tannour charcoal overnight method; altulou fortieth-day birth distribution; completion of Quran celebrated with harees.
jafnah|Abu Dhabi Culture — Jafnah|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/jafnah|Deep wooden communal food bowl; called yafnah locally; large bowls for feasts and Ramadan.
jallaf|Abu Dhabi Culture — Jallaf|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/jallaf|Shipwright; oustad master; historic planks sewn with coconut fibre; kalafat inserts grease-soaked cotton between planks; shalamen trims boards; nailer fixes nails.
judoor|Abu Dhabi Culture — Judoor|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/judoor|Plural jadr pots; pottery oldest widespread; metal vessels copper/brass/aluminium later.
khous|Abu Dhabi Culture — Khous|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/khous|Palm-leaf weaving; coarse leaves soaked to soften; tools bodkin needle scissors water bowl; inner leaves for surood mekhrafa jafeer; dyed water colours leaves.
qassab|Abu Dhabi Culture — Qassab|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/qassab|Butcher; slaughter site maqssab; sakeeks narrow residential alleys; traditional meat trade busy in Ramadan.
serai|Abu Dhabi Culture — Serai|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/serai|Kerosene lamp; wick draws fuel; transparent glass enclosure farsha.
furniture|Abu Dhabi Culture — Traditional home furniture|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/traditional-home-furniture|Mandoos wooden clothes and valuables chest mainly India imports; legs avoid damp; copper decorations; sahharah metal chest; mawasid cushions; haseer palm mat.
zuhba|Abu Dhabi Culture — Zuhba|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/zuhba|Bridal trousseau gold clothing perfume supplied groom family; meer food provisions; suwaia silk abaya; neighbourhood women sew; wedding jewellery includes kawashi murtaasha hiyool.
henna|Abu Dhabi Culture — Henna|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/henna|Leaf paste decoration; minhaz pounding; ghamsa full hand front/back; rawayeb fingertip pattern; sheraa triangular pattern. Medical claims not used.
kohl|Abu Dhabi Culture — Kohl|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/kohl|Eye adornment; athmad stone-based; saray soot-based; makhala storage vessel; mirwad applicator; traditional men and women use. Medical claims not used.
majlis|Abu Dhabi Culture — Majlis|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/majlis|Community gathering/discussion; barza elders' majlis; merchants finance divers; justice majlis resolves legal cases; inscribed2015 with Oman Qatar Saudi Arabia.
eid|Abu Dhabi Culture — Celebrating Eid|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/celebrating-eid|Fitr after Ramadan; Adha linked Haj; visiting family and charity; new clothes henna; Bedouin first snack dates and milk.
wanna|Abu Dhabi Culture — Wanna|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/wanna|Melodic Nabati singing conveys sadness longing calm; sometimes singers exchange lines; part of Ayyala.
nabati|Abu Dhabi Culture — Nabati poetry|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/oral-expressions/nabati-poetry|Colloquial Arabic poetry; referenced by Ibn Khaldun Muqaddimah in14th century; Million's Poet TV competition; advice riddles praise longing.
falcon|Abu Dhabi Culture — Falconry|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-performing-arts/falconry|Traditional hunting; feather decoy training; leather hood covers eyes; forearm guard; wooden perch; pigeons live training; Sheikh Zayed release programme and Falcon Hospital.
saluki|Abu Dhabi Culture — Saluki dogs|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-performing-arts/saluki-dogs|Bedouin hunting/guard dogs; Hoss and Aryash coat types; work alongside falcons retrieving hidden prey; Arabian Saluki Centre Abu Dhabi2001; competition values character intelligence hunting skills.
dahrouj|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Dahrouj game|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/oral-expressions/the-game-of-al-dahrouj|Children run after rolling wheel; palm-frond version wind-powered; finish-line winner.
karabi|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Karabi game|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/oral-expressions/the-game-of-al-karabi|Hopping one leg while holding bent other leg; cross and return between lines without falling while opponents obstruct.
suwair|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Suwair game|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/oral-expressions/the-game-of-al-suwair|Two teams; Ramadan moonlit chasing game; houl enclosed area; leader Suwair call; capture swaps roles.
essee|Abu Dhabi Culture — Es Es See game|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/oral-expressions/the-game-of-es-es-see|Two girls facing each other rhythmically clap palms with chanting.
tabat|Abu Dhabi Culture — Gol Tabat game|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/oral-expressions/the-game-of-gol-tabat|Riddle game questioner gives answer when opponent says Gol Jeej; Gol tabat indicates inability to answer.
maryahana|Abu Dhabi Culture — Maryahanat Al Badw|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/oral-expressions/the-game-of-maryahanat-al-badw|Two seated players facing holding hands alternate pulling back to ground; songs accompany.
meendarabak|Abu Dhabi Culture — Meen Darabak game|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/oral-expressions/the-game-of-meen-darabak|Covered eyes player identifies shoulder tapper; correct guess switches roles; no equipment.
motor|Abu Dhabi Culture — Motor Bou Ajal|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/oral-expressions/the-game-of-motor-bou-ajal|Children make toy cars from wires empty tins; small tin lids wheels.
dress|Dubai Tourism — Wulfa fashion guide|https://www.visitdubai.com/ar/festivals-and-events/-/media/files/faqs/wulfa/wulfa-guide-to-emirati-fashion.pdf|Kandura robe; wizar waist cloth; faneela undergarment; sudairi sleeveless winter vest; ghafiya cap; ghutra scarf; agal black securing cord; medas sandals.
dressbasic|Dubai Tourism — National dress|https://www.visitdubai.com/ar/-/media/Images/pdf/2025/city-guides/dubai-city-guide-2025-sun-and-sand-seeker.pdf|Women's abaya outer garment; ghutra desert protection; agal holds scarf; burqa mask.
coffeecustom|UNESCO — Arabic coffee|https://ich.unesco.org/en/RL/arabic-coffee-a-symbol-of-generosity-02111|Older people/guests served first; pour with right hand; shake cup finished; original2015 inscription extended Jordan2024.
hedaa|UNESCO — Alhedaa|https://ich.unesco.org/en/RL/alheda-a-oral-traditions-of-calling-camel-flocks-01717?RL=01717|Herders rhythmic calls communicate with camels; assemble swiftly sandstorm; right-left/kneeling trained; inscription2022 UAE Oman Saudi Arabia.
sadu|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Sadu|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/heritage-carousel/al-sadu|Camel hair goat hair sheep wool; women weave floor loom from palm; textiles tents rugs saddle adornment.
foodguide|Dubai Tourism — Wulfa season guide|https://www.visitdubai.com/en/festivals-and-events/-/media/Files/faqs/wulfa/wulfa-guide-to-the-season.pdf|Luqaimat fried dough with date syrup or honey; balaleet sweet vermicelli and fried eggs; thareed meat vegetables over bread; machboos spiced rice meat; khanfaroosh fried saffron cardamom pastry; maleh salted sun-dried fish; bajella fava beans dango chickpeas.
fwala|Dubai Tourism — Emirati fwala guide|https://www.visitdubai.com/en/festivals-and-events/-/media/files/faqs/wulfa/wulfa-guide-to-emirati-fwala.pdf|Fwala Emirati afternoon hospitality spread; khameer fluffy bread with chami; aseeda cooked flour with ghee or honey; coffee cardamom saffron.
ayyala|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Ayyala|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/unesco-ich-inscribed-elements/al-ayyala|Two facing rows; bamboo canes represent swords/arrows; Nabati poetry of valour; yaweela circle; UNESCO2014; regional rhythm variations.
razfa|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Razfa|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/unesco-ich-inscribed-elements/al-razfa|Two facing rows; razeefa men and boys; naashat young women swaying hair; earlier swords or daggers; UNESCO2015; new poems composed for occasions.
talli|Abu Dhabi Culture — Talli|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/unesco-ich-inscribed-elements/talli|Braided strips adorn women's clothing; mousadah pillow on kajoujah stand; dahary bobbins; silver/gold central thread; sayer yaay back-and-forth; bu-khostain two silver bobbins versus bu-khosa one.
taghrooda|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Taghrooda|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/unesco-ich-inscribed-elements/al-taghrooda|Improvised camel-rider Bedouin poetry; short poems seven or fewer lines repeated alternately; UNESCO2012; social bonds; Obaid Ibn Maaaded Al Nuaimi from Al Wajan.
azi|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Azi|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/unesco-ich-inscribed-elements/al-azi|Poetic recitation with responding men; no musical/percussion accompaniment; UNESCO urgent safeguarding2017; rhymed verses interspersed proverbs.
coffee|Abu Dhabi Culture — Gahwa publication|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-resources/publications/gahwa-arabic-coffee|Dallah coffee pot; khumrah large boiling pot; talgeemah medium filtering pot; mazalah small serving pot; dallah left hand cup right; quarter-full cup; guest right hand.
haqlaila|UAE Ministry of Culture — Haq Al Laila|https://moc.gov.ae/en/news/haq-al-laila-convoy-tours-the-uae-to-celebrate-the-popular-tradition/|Mid-Shaaban celebration night15 welcomes Ramadan; children collect sweets and nuts from neighbourhood houses in traditional dress.
oasislife|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Ain educator resource|https://abudhabiculture.ae/-/media/project/abudhabiculture/abudhabiculture/documents/alainculturalsiteseducatorresourceenglish2025.pdf|Fazaa rushing to help; shared building harvesting and aflaj cleaning; areesh temporary palm-frond/branch houses; mud brick clay mortar and palm ceilings.
fahidi|Dubai Tourism — Al Fahidi|https://www.visitdubai.com/places-to-visit/al-fahidi-historical-neighbourhood|Traditional wind-tower district on Dubai Creek; mid19th century life; teak gypsum sandstone palm and sandalwood construction.
dhayah|Ras Al Khaimah Tourism — Dhayah Fort|https://visitrasalkhaimah.com/discover/attractions/dhayah-fort/|RAK hilltop fort; 1819 battle Qawasim and British; current fortress19th century;239 steps; oasis watchtowers; Wadi Suq tombs.
dhayahhistory|Ras Al Khaimah Tourism — Dhayah heritage brochure|https://visitrasalkhaimah.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/Dhayah.pdf|Hill fort temporary defence lacked water; larger lower refuge called Sur protected people and animals; two towers face courtyard;1990s restoration.
sharjahfort|Sharjah Tourism — Heritage district|https://blog.visitsharjah.com/en/48-hours-in-sharjah|Sharjah fort built1823; government seat and ruler residence; coral stone teak palms; Bait Al Naboodah pearl merchant home; Heart of Sharjah evokes1950s.
jahili|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Jahili Fort|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/Cultural-Sites/Historic-Buildings-And-Cultural-Landscapes/Al-Jahili-Fort|Zayed bin Khalifa Zayed First commissioned; summer residence;1891 to1898; four-tier round tower; three corner towers fourth majlis; Thesiger permanent exhibition;1950s British headquarters.
aflaj|Abu Dhabi Culture — Al Aflaj|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/unesco-ich-inscribed-elements/al-aflaj|Underground irrigation tunnels reduce evaporation; gravity via gradual gradient; surface channels to farms; equitable water distribution and community clearing mud; UNESCO2020.
camelrace|Abu Dhabi Culture — Camel racing|https://abudhabiculture.ae/en/cultural-heritage/intangible/unesco-ich-inscribed-elements/camel-feeding|Racing distance based on camel age; preparation committee verifies origin; training groups; UNESCO2020.
fishingar|Abu Dhabi Culture — أدوات صيد الأسماك|https://abudhabiculture.ae/ar/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/fishing-equipment|Arabic original calls the iron bottom weight of kufa صنجل; English transliteration Sinjil, with Sanjal another rendering.
saqaar|Abu Dhabi Culture — السقا|https://abudhabiculture.ae/ar/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/the-saqa|Three wooden supports make the mashadd also called tarjabah; the separate upper pole is shayb; mouth waja.
burqaar|Abu Dhabi Culture — البرقع|https://abudhabiculture.ae/ar/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/burqa|Craft name قرض البراقع; red sheel lining expensive; seif nose bridge; shubuq ties.
rahaar|Abu Dhabi Culture — الرحى|https://abudhabiculture.ae/ar/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/al-raha|Original Arabic الثقال denotes woven cloth beneath mill; qutb axis; hadi handle; tarsha heavy mill.
utensilsar|Abu Dhabi Culture — أدوات طهي الطعام|https://abudhabiculture.ae/ar/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/cooking-utensils|Original Arabic الكفشة also الخاشوقة is large serving spoon; tabi frying pan; mashkhala strainer.
sandalwoodar|Abu Dhabi Culture — خشب الصندل|https://abudhabiculture.ae/ar/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/traditional-handicraft/sandalwood|Hair powder البضاعة includes crushed sandalwood wars rose mahaleb; no treatment claims used.
maritimear|Abu Dhabi Culture — الحياة البحرية|https://abudhabiculture.ae/ar/cultural-heritage/intangible/heritage-register/social-practices/maritime-life|Saffar and qatta are vessel types for long and short trading trips respectively; boum common sailing merchant vessel; palm-fibre ropes; noora hull coating.
